WEBVTT

00:12.150 --> 00:14.820
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

00:15.660 --> 00:19.030
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are Super Adorable!</b>

01:27.190 --> 01:29.980
Super Cute Angels ♥

01:27.190 --> 01:29.980
<b>Hokkaido Gals Are</b>

01:27.190 --> 01:29.980
<b>Boom!</b>

01:27.190 --> 01:29.980
<b>Super Adorable</b>

01:30.650 --> 01:35.320
<b>Episode 10:
Time Flies Super Fast</b>

01:30.650 --> 01:35.320
<b>Episode 10:
Time Flies Super Fast</b>

01:40.410 --> 01:45.120
<i>At Tokyo's Ueno Park, the cherry 
blossoms are already in full bloom</i>

01:45.120 --> 01:47.330
<i>and are attracting many visitors.</i>

01:45.610 --> 01:47.330
Cherry blossoms, huh?

01:49.890 --> 01:52.170
<i>Although it has warmed up somewhat now,</i>

01:53.960 --> 01:57.220
<i>spring in Hokkaido is still pretty cold.</i>

01:58.520 --> 02:00.310
Okay, I'm heading out.

02:00.310 --> 02:02.520
Take care. I'll see you later.

02:10.360 --> 02:11.770
Hurry up!

02:13.190 --> 02:15.210
I guess I'm in second year now.

02:16.010 --> 02:20.070
<i>When I came to Hokkaido, 
the snow-covered roads really surprised me.</i>

02:20.070 --> 02:22.790
<i>But I guess it already has been two months.</i>

02:23.320 --> 02:25.080
<i>Time really does fly.</i>

02:31.350 --> 02:33.040
<i>It's Fuyuki-san.</i>

02:33.040 --> 02:36.670
<i>But isn't this out of the 
way coming from her place?</i>

02:38.590 --> 02:40.390
Oh, Tsubasa!

02:40.390 --> 02:42.010
Good morning, Fuyuki-san.

02:42.010 --> 02:43.510
You finally got here!

02:43.510 --> 02:45.290
Huh? Finally?

02:46.680 --> 02:50.440
I was waiting for you so we 
could walk to school together.

02:51.070 --> 02:53.440
Even though it is getting warmer,

02:53.440 --> 02:56.660
making a young maiden wait alone 
in the cold air like this...?

02:56.660 --> 02:58.360
What an cruel man you are!

02:58.360 --> 03:02.830
I-I'm sorry! If you had told me, 
I could have left earlier.

03:02.830 --> 03:05.280
Huh? Not a chance!

03:05.280 --> 03:08.690
I wanted to get to see that 
surprised look on your face.

03:08.690 --> 03:10.380
Uh, okay.

03:11.350 --> 03:15.620
<i>Fuyuki-san is really on the offensive today for some reason.</i>

03:15.620 --> 03:17.910
So like, is your cold better now?

03:18.450 --> 03:21.580
Oh, yeah. I'm perfectly fine now.

03:22.100 --> 03:27.970
But Grandma got worried after that and 
told me I have to be in bed by 9:00.

03:28.660 --> 03:32.750
So for the second half of spring break, 
I was living really healthy

03:32.750 --> 03:35.460
but I couldn't go on any 
big trips or anything.

03:35.460 --> 03:37.980
I feel so bad for you.

03:38.200 --> 03:40.880
But you gotta listen to your granny.

03:40.880 --> 03:43.570
Yeah. I really should be thankful.

03:45.690 --> 03:49.450
My spring break went by in a flash, too.

03:49.780 --> 03:51.030
Were you that busy?

03:51.030 --> 03:52.180
Mm-hmm.

03:52.180 --> 03:55.150
But to tell the truth, over spring break

03:57.160 --> 04:00.300
I wish I could have spent a lot 
more time with you, Tsubasa.

04:01.550 --> 04:06.200
Ah! Your heart just skipped a beat, right? 
You're so easy to read!

04:06.200 --> 04:08.590
Well... I mean...

04:08.590 --> 04:11.560
<i>First day of the term and 
she's coming on so strong!</i>

04:13.690 --> 04:16.470
Hokkaido sure is impressive, though.

04:16.470 --> 04:17.450
What do you mean?

04:17.450 --> 04:20.530
It's already April, but there's 
still snow on the ground.

04:20.960 --> 04:24.780
Everyone in Tokyo thinks April 
is all about cherry blossoms.

04:25.050 --> 04:28.840
Tokyo is in full bloom, right? 
I saw it on TV this morning.

04:29.460 --> 04:32.460
Up here, cherry blossoms bloom around May,

04:32.460 --> 04:34.790
so we don't think about them 
as part of the new school year.

04:34.790 --> 04:35.950
Oh, really?

04:35.950 --> 04:39.830
But instead, cherry and plum and peach 
trees all bloom at the same time!

04:39.830 --> 04:41.610
Huh? That's crazy!

04:41.610 --> 04:44.300
Spring comes and then goes just like that!

04:44.840 --> 04:48.520
It feels like winter ends and 
then all of a sudden it's summer.

04:48.520 --> 04:49.810
Huh...

04:49.810 --> 04:53.210
I'm not sure if that sounds better or worse.

04:53.620 --> 04:58.120
For me, out of all four seasons, 
spring is my favorite.

04:58.430 --> 05:02.940
I guess I probably like winter best. 
There's a lot that happens.

05:03.360 --> 05:07.320
Skiing, right? 
The winter yakiniku festival, right?

05:07.320 --> 05:13.330
Then Christmas, New Year's, 
and even Valentine's Day!

05:13.330 --> 05:15.850
Yeah, you have a point.

05:21.990 --> 05:25.190
I do want to see Hokkaido's 
cherry blossoms soon, though.

05:28.560 --> 05:30.210
Oh, that's right.

05:30.210 --> 05:34.100
We get our new class assignments today. 
I hope we get in the same class again.

05:34.520 --> 05:35.720
I do, too.

05:36.220 --> 05:39.530
<i>Huh? Fuyuki-san seems sad all of a sudden.</i>

05:39.900 --> 05:43.480
I heard a rumor that when classes 
get assigned at our school,

05:43.480 --> 05:47.770
students with good grades and students 
with bad grades don't get placed together.

05:47.770 --> 05:49.590
What? Really?

05:49.590 --> 05:50.410
Yeah.

05:50.410 --> 05:54.570
They didn't tell me that during 
orientation when I transferred, though.

05:54.570 --> 05:57.760
It is just a rumor, so I don't 
know if it's true or not.

05:58.570 --> 06:00.820
But if it is true, you know,

06:01.290 --> 06:05.420
I might not get into the same class as you.

06:06.810 --> 06:08.090
Fuyuki-san...

06:10.680 --> 06:14.680
If we get into different classes, 
we won't see each other as much.

06:15.110 --> 06:18.290
We'd probably make new friends in class, too.

06:19.000 --> 06:23.780
When I started thinking about that, 
it made me kinda sad.

06:24.700 --> 06:29.860
That's why I wanted to walk 
to school with you today.

06:33.790 --> 06:36.290
Even if we do get into different classes,

06:37.200 --> 06:39.040
I'll go visit you, Fuyuki-san!

06:40.960 --> 06:44.750
So, I mean... how do I put this...

06:44.750 --> 06:46.710
You can put your mind at ease...?

06:48.810 --> 06:52.660
Um, or maybe not ease, but I'm 
not going to let you worry...?

06:52.660 --> 06:56.520
<i>Whoa! Everything coming out of 
my mouth sounds so embarrassing!</i>

06:59.210 --> 07:01.900
Tsubasa, you're trying 
so hard to play it cool!

07:01.900 --> 07:05.360
And you're making yourself blush! Hilarious!

07:05.360 --> 07:09.710
<i>I know I am! Damn it!</i>

07:11.520 --> 07:13.330
But still, thank you.

07:13.330 --> 07:17.290
Thanks to you, Tsubasa, 
I don't feel sad anymore!

07:20.080 --> 07:21.540
Let's hurry up and get to school.

07:21.540 --> 07:22.360
Yeah!

07:25.130 --> 07:29.420
Year 2 Class 4

07:25.450 --> 07:29.420
Okay, um... A, Ka, Sa, Shi...

07:29.420 --> 07:30.840
Where's Shiki now.

07:30.840 --> 07:32.810
Fuyuki, Fuyuki...

07:32.780 --> 07:34.600
<b>Shiki
Tsubasa</b>

07:32.900 --> 07:34.600
<b>Fuyuki
Minami</b>

07:33.630 --> 07:34.600
Oh.

07:34.600 --> 07:35.660
There I am!

07:35.660 --> 07:37.260
Year 2 class 4!

07:37.770 --> 07:40.250
Huh? The same class?!

07:38.560 --> 07:40.230
Year 2 Class 4

07:40.250 --> 07:41.840
Yes, Fuyuki-san!

07:41.840 --> 07:43.150
Hooray!

07:43.150 --> 07:45.360
So that rumor was all wrong!

07:45.610 --> 07:47.270
Let's have a great class together!

07:47.270 --> 07:48.620
For sure, for sure!

07:48.620 --> 07:50.250
Shiki! Fuyuki!

07:51.200 --> 07:52.950
We're in the same class again.

07:52.950 --> 07:54.280
You, too, Akino-san?

07:54.280 --> 07:55.620
Class 4?

07:55.620 --> 08:01.500
I'm in the same class as Sayurin again! 
I'm super surprised and happy!

08:01.500 --> 08:05.170
Well, I always figured we'd 
be in the same class again.

08:05.170 --> 08:07.780
Amaz— Are you psychic or something?

08:07.780 --> 08:11.520
And here I was so worried about it.

08:11.520 --> 08:12.170
Worried?

08:12.170 --> 08:13.090
Mm-hmm.

08:13.090 --> 08:17.100
There was a rumor that students would 
be grouped together by test grades.

08:17.100 --> 08:19.140
Yeah, I heard that.

08:19.140 --> 08:20.680
Oh, you did?

08:20.680 --> 08:24.940
But if they were placing students by grades, 
they would've done that from the start.

08:24.940 --> 08:28.320
Come on, Sayurin. 
How can you be so chill about it?

08:29.410 --> 08:30.440
Huh?

08:30.440 --> 08:32.110
Sayurin, did you cut your hair?

08:32.110 --> 08:34.660
Huh? Uh, yeah.

08:35.390 --> 08:37.210
Just to make it a little lighter.

08:39.910 --> 08:41.560
It's perfect for spring!

08:41.560 --> 08:43.430
Don't you think so, Tsubasa?

08:43.430 --> 08:44.210
Yeah!

08:44.210 --> 08:47.130
I think you look really great, Akino-san!

08:47.130 --> 08:48.240
Uh...

08:48.980 --> 08:49.690
Huh?

08:50.340 --> 08:53.090
Oh, sorry. Did I say something weird?

08:53.090 --> 08:54.320
N-No, I—

08:54.320 --> 08:55.360
Hey!

08:55.960 --> 08:57.130
Mat-tsun!

08:59.130 --> 09:03.680
I'm in class 2-4, too. 
Let's have a great year, guys!

09:03.680 --> 09:06.370
You're in the same class?

09:06.370 --> 09:09.940
I'm so happy I'm together with 
a bunch of my friends again.

09:09.940 --> 09:12.320
It would suck to be all alone from the start.

09:12.320 --> 09:13.300
Mm-hmm!

09:13.300 --> 09:14.730
Yeah, I'm so relieved!

09:15.750 --> 09:17.470
Let's get to class, man.

09:17.470 --> 09:19.260
Oh. Huh?

09:21.620 --> 09:24.490
Now I can keep teaching 
you about games, Shiki.

09:24.490 --> 09:27.870
Yes, Professor! I look forward to 
continuing my studies with you!

09:28.430 --> 09:32.610
I just heard all about the new update. 
We've gotta make the most of it!

09:32.610 --> 09:34.720
What? Akino-san, you play video games?

09:36.140 --> 09:38.640
What exactly do you mean "play"?

09:38.640 --> 09:41.760
Oh, no, no! It's just that I like games, too.

09:43.980 --> 09:50.270
I play anything. Battle royale-type FPS 
games, rhythm games, even All Climb.

09:50.650 --> 09:52.650
Man, that's a pretty sick lineup.

09:52.650 --> 09:55.630
After you eat something sweet, 
you're gonna want something salty, right?

09:55.630 --> 09:56.700
Oh, definitely.

09:56.700 --> 10:00.370
You understand what she meant? 
You guys sure are close.

10:00.370 --> 10:02.530
Oh. Okay then, do you play Sis-Plus?

10:01.680 --> 10:02.530
Fuyuki-san.

10:02.530 --> 10:03.830
Oh, I totally do.

10:04.210 --> 10:04.950
Let's go.

10:09.190 --> 10:09.910
Yeah!

10:16.990 --> 10:23.600
<b>Toguchi Misa</b>

10:17.370 --> 10:19.880
Hello, everyone. 
Welcome to the new school year!

10:20.290 --> 10:23.600
I'm your homeroom teacher, Toguchi Misa.

10:23.600 --> 10:26.220
Let's all have a wonderful year together!

10:27.010 --> 10:29.910
Well then, for our first 
homeroom class today,

10:29.910 --> 10:33.520
I'd like us to select a class 
president and vice president.

10:33.520 --> 10:36.690
First of all, would anyone like 
to volunteer as a candidate?

10:36.690 --> 10:38.610
You can also nominate 
someone else if you wish.

10:40.030 --> 10:41.630
I do, Teacher!

10:41.630 --> 10:43.200
Yes, Matsuo-kun?

10:43.200 --> 10:46.370
For class president, 
I think Shiki would be best!

10:46.370 --> 10:47.160
Huh?!

10:47.160 --> 10:49.610
Would you mind explaining 
why you're nominating him?

10:49.610 --> 10:54.190
Well, okay. Shiki is super 
smart and really responsible.

10:54.190 --> 10:56.670
He's a great guy all around who 
really cares about his friends!

10:56.890 --> 11:00.610
Um, but I only transferred 
here half a year ago.

11:00.610 --> 11:02.340
That doesn't matter!

11:02.790 --> 11:07.220
If Shiki became president, I know he 
wouldn't try to run everything himself.

11:07.220 --> 11:11.690
He'd listen to everyone's opinions carefully 
and turn this into a really great class!

11:11.990 --> 11:15.440
<i>Is that how you see me, Matsuo-kun?</i>

11:15.440 --> 11:17.240
I agree with that!

11:17.240 --> 11:18.150
So do I.

11:18.150 --> 11:20.450
Oh! Two more supporters!

11:22.430 --> 11:24.600
Also, he's from Tokyo!

11:24.600 --> 11:27.540
I-Is that a reason to nominate me?

11:27.540 --> 11:31.770
Well then, Shiki-kun, 
how do you feel about that?

11:31.770 --> 11:34.290
Do you have any interest in being president?

11:34.290 --> 11:35.700
Well...

11:37.040 --> 11:41.670
If it means I can help everyone out, 
then I guess I could give it a shot.

11:41.670 --> 11:43.180
Yes!

11:41.670 --> 11:43.510
Wow!

11:43.510 --> 11:47.840
If there aren't any other candidates, 
then we'll settle on Shiki-kun.

11:47.840 --> 11:49.690
Is there anyone else?

11:49.690 --> 11:51.690
No, there isn't!

11:51.690 --> 11:54.700
Well then, Shiki-kun, the duty is yours.

11:54.700 --> 11:56.130
A-All right.

11:56.130 --> 11:58.600
<i>They decided so quickly!</i>

11:58.600 --> 12:00.340
And next, for the vice pres—

12:00.340 --> 12:01.780
Me, me, me!

12:01.780 --> 12:03.940
I'll do it!

12:03.940 --> 12:05.200
Seriously?!

12:07.230 --> 12:08.810
We have a volunteer.

12:08.810 --> 12:10.650
What do you think, everyone?

12:10.650 --> 12:13.540
Hey, hey. Fuyumina, you gonna be okay?

12:13.540 --> 12:15.130
Yeah, of course I am!

12:15.130 --> 12:17.960
Despite my looks, I'm super responsible!

12:17.960 --> 12:19.980
I can only imagine you as a gyaru.

12:19.980 --> 12:22.210
Yeah, a responsible gyaru!

12:24.100 --> 12:28.020
Everyone, please congratulate your new 
class president and vice president.

12:24.780 --> 12:29.890
<b>President Shiki</b>

12:24.780 --> 12:29.890
<b>Vice President Fuyuki Minami</b>

12:30.330 --> 12:34.140
I'm glad that was decided so smoothly. 
That makes me very happy.

12:34.140 --> 12:36.090
I'm super happy about it, too!

12:48.090 --> 12:49.330
<b>Shiki</b>

12:48.280 --> 12:49.330
Oh! It's him!

12:49.330 --> 12:51.710
Um, can you hear me, Akino-san?

12:51.710 --> 12:53.390
<i>Uh, yeah. I can hear you.</i>

12:53.390 --> 12:55.750
Oh good. Then I guess it's working.

12:55.750 --> 12:59.040
Didn't you say this was your 
first time playing online?

12:59.040 --> 13:01.510
<i>Yeah! I've been looking forward to it!</i>

13:01.850 --> 13:03.840
Um, the game is called...

13:03.840 --> 13:06.090
<i>All Together! Monster Climbing</i>.

13:03.840 --> 13:08.090
<b>All Together! Monster Climbing</b>

13:06.090 --> 13:07.770
<i>Or </i>All Climb<i> for short.</i>

13:08.090 --> 13:12.330
But you didn't have a game 
console until recently, right?

13:12.330 --> 13:13.360
What happened?

13:13.360 --> 13:16.300
<i>I had some allowance saved 
up and bought it with that.</i>

13:17.120 --> 13:19.180
Oh, man, I'm so sorry!

13:19.180 --> 13:22.580
I thought everyone in the 
world already owned a console,

13:22.580 --> 13:24.230
so I invited you without considering that.

13:24.230 --> 13:25.710
<i>Don't worry about it!</i>

13:25.710 --> 13:28.360
<i>I was interested in one anyway, 
so it was perfect timing.</i>

13:30.200 --> 13:34.490
Shiki, you never say "no" when people 
invite you for stuff. Why is that?

13:34.490 --> 13:36.210
<i>Huh? Oh...</i>

13:36.890 --> 13:41.210
Well, you never know if something is 
interesting or fun until you give it a try.

13:41.670 --> 13:43.510
So I'm really glad you asked me to play.

13:47.900 --> 13:51.960
Shiki, I want to invite you to my mountain. 
What's your character's name?

13:51.960 --> 13:53.650
<i>Hanekoto.</i>

13:53.650 --> 13:55.160
"Hane," like feather?

13:55.160 --> 13:57.270
Oh, because "Tsubasa" means wing!

13:57.270 --> 13:58.540
What about yours?

14:00.350 --> 14:01.260
<i>Tamu-san.</i>

14:01.260 --> 14:03.330
Tamu-san? But why?

14:03.330 --> 14:06.880
<i>Shiki! It's off limits to ask someone 
about the origin of their character name!</i>

14:06.880 --> 14:08.200
I-I'm sorry!

14:08.200 --> 14:11.460
<i>Y-You're right. 
I think it's a really cute name.</i>

14:12.820 --> 14:14.700
Am I doing this the right way?

14:14.700 --> 14:17.540
You're good. This is my house.

14:17.540 --> 14:21.040
Huh? You've got an amazing house, Tamu-san!

14:21.040 --> 14:23.130
Y-You really think so?

14:24.160 --> 14:26.590
Wow! This is great!

14:26.590 --> 14:30.530
Didn't it take a ton of work 
to get each piece of furniture?

14:31.450 --> 14:35.770
Yeah, well, when I get down to business, 
this is sort of what happens.

14:36.750 --> 14:39.270
<i>B-But there's one thing I should tell you.</i>

14:39.530 --> 14:41.530
Nobody's ever come to my house before.

14:41.530 --> 14:44.370
Shi—Hanekoto, you're the first one.

14:45.770 --> 14:49.300
I am? Really? Then this really is an honor.

14:49.300 --> 14:50.740
Thank you for the invitation!

14:50.740 --> 14:54.090
<i>It's just a game but I'm 
getting so nervous! Why?</i>

14:54.090 --> 14:56.790
W-Well then, do you want to 
come over to my place, too?

14:57.480 --> 14:59.580
U-Um, okay.

15:01.250 --> 15:04.370
Uh... So it's basically 
still the original settings?

15:04.370 --> 15:06.250
Sorry it's so dull.

15:06.500 --> 15:11.180
I did get a special bonus when I bought 
it that gave me this weird mascot, though.

15:11.180 --> 15:15.100
As long as you like it, Hanekoto, 
it's good enough for me. Yeah.

15:15.100 --> 15:20.440
I've thought about changing things, 
but I don't have enough materials yet.

15:20.440 --> 15:22.270
Or any design skill.

15:22.650 --> 15:25.990
Then why don't you come to my 
mountain to gather materials?

15:25.990 --> 15:27.850
<i>Huh? Can I?</i>

15:27.850 --> 15:29.600
<i>Thank you, Tamu-san!</i>

15:30.700 --> 15:34.700
Mt. Taisetsu

15:34.700 --> 15:36.700
Mt. Taisetsu?

15:34.700 --> 15:38.410
<b>Mt. Taisetsu</b>

15:36.700 --> 15:38.410
That's kind of a cute name.

15:38.410 --> 15:42.000
<i>Yeah. It's the name of 
a mountain in Hokkaido.</i>

15:42.410 --> 15:43.900
<i>It's called Taisetsu-zan.</i>

15:43.900 --> 15:48.590
Oh. The one you spell with the 
characters for "heavy snow," right?

15:48.590 --> 15:51.010
I always thought it was 
pronounced Daisetsu-zan.

15:51.010 --> 15:53.680
This is "taisetsu" because it's 
Tamu-san's "special" mountain, right?

15:53.680 --> 15:54.440
Oh...

15:53.680 --> 16:00.180
<b>Jaga Pokkuru</b>

15:55.430 --> 15:58.300
Well, I suppose you could 
pronounce it either way.

16:26.920 --> 16:27.920
Wow!

16:28.490 --> 16:32.000
We already got a bunch! 
All thanks to you, Tamu-san!

16:32.000 --> 16:34.930
For a beginner, you're pretty 
good yourself, Hanekoto.

16:34.930 --> 16:36.300
<b>Mt. Taisetsu</b>

16:34.930 --> 16:36.300
<b>Hanekoto's Mountain</b>

16:46.040 --> 16:48.590
Now we just have to wait for it to finish.

16:48.590 --> 16:52.280
But I went ahead and already did a 
bunch of stuff. I hope that was okay.

16:52.280 --> 16:55.210
I'm actually grateful for all the help.

16:55.210 --> 16:57.690
I would've run out of steam 
if I had to do it myself.

16:57.690 --> 16:59.940
<i>Really? Then I'm glad.</i>

16:59.940 --> 17:02.200
You really are amazing, Tamu-san.

17:02.450 --> 17:03.370
<i>Thank you!</i>

17:06.350 --> 17:07.050
<i>No.</i>

17:07.050 --> 17:07.830
Huh?

17:07.830 --> 17:10.070
<i>You and Fuyuki are way more amazing.</i>

17:10.070 --> 17:10.730
Huh?

17:11.130 --> 17:12.240
So is Matsuo.

17:12.680 --> 17:16.260
It was his first time in our class today, and he 
had the guts to nominate you for president?

17:16.470 --> 17:19.530
Matsuo-kun really is outgoing, isn't he?

17:19.530 --> 17:22.380
<i>It was awesome that you accepted 
after you were nominated,</i>

17:22.380 --> 17:25.110
<i>and awesome that Fuyuki volunteered 
to be vice president just like that.</i>

17:25.660 --> 17:28.230
I was really surprised 
when Fuyuki-san did that.

17:30.330 --> 17:31.300
<i>Akino-san?</i>

17:32.470 --> 17:34.650
You're all just so great.

17:35.530 --> 17:39.470
And here I am, same as always. 
I haven't changed a bit.

17:39.470 --> 17:42.200
<i>Are you sure? I think you have.</i>

17:42.200 --> 17:43.120
Huh?

17:43.360 --> 17:48.500
You always used to isolate yourself, 
but then when you talked to me,

17:48.750 --> 17:52.090
and when you decided to try skiing 
down that mountain in class,

17:52.090 --> 17:55.840
I think those things show 
that you've changed a lot.

17:55.840 --> 17:57.150
Those were just...

17:57.150 --> 17:58.800
<i>There's a lot of other stuff too.</i>

17:59.200 --> 18:03.010
When Fuyuki-san and I were total beginners, 
you taught us how to play games.

18:03.500 --> 18:07.140
When Matsuo-kun said something mean 
to Fuyuki-san, you got angry at him.

18:10.500 --> 18:13.820
Well, if I really have changed, 
then it's all thanks—

18:13.820 --> 18:15.860
<i>Oh! It's done!</i>

18:20.300 --> 18:24.120
Oh, sorry! Weren't you about 
to say something, Akino-san?

18:25.090 --> 18:25.910
Nah.

18:26.420 --> 18:28.080
<i>Good luck being class president.</i>

18:29.420 --> 18:30.970
I'll be rooting for you.

18:40.640 --> 18:42.430
<b>Storage Room</b>

18:46.490 --> 18:49.220
Once we get all the print-outs 
together, we're done.

18:49.580 --> 18:52.090
It's already starting to get dark outside.

18:52.090 --> 18:53.560
Oh, you're right.

18:53.560 --> 18:56.250
Isn't it fun being in 
school at night like this?

18:56.250 --> 18:59.650
Eh... I don't think it's really my thing.

18:59.650 --> 19:03.760
Oh? Are you scared of ghosts 
or something, Tsuba-cha?

19:03.760 --> 19:08.690
No, that's not what I mean. 
It's just... really dark and quiet.

19:08.690 --> 19:11.500
When nobody's around, it gets kind of lonely.

19:11.500 --> 19:12.960
That's why I like it.

19:12.960 --> 19:13.700
Huh?

19:13.700 --> 19:17.670
'Cause I mean, it feels like we're 
the only people in the whole world.

19:17.670 --> 19:19.630
Doesn't that get your heart beating?

19:33.700 --> 19:36.620
I-I forgot something! I meant to thank you!

19:36.620 --> 19:38.340
Thank me? For what?

19:38.340 --> 19:41.150
For volunteering to be vice president.

19:41.670 --> 19:44.240
It was a surprise, but it actually helps a ton.

19:44.240 --> 19:48.590
Oh, right. Everybody tells 
me it was a surprise!

19:48.590 --> 19:50.830
Do I really seem that unreliable?

19:50.830 --> 19:53.420
No, no, it's not that you aren't reliable.

19:53.680 --> 19:57.190
It just seemed like something 
you wouldn't be interested in.

19:57.190 --> 20:01.380
Well, I guess I have never done it before.

20:01.380 --> 20:04.140
I always thought I wouldn't 
like doing this stuff.

20:04.140 --> 20:06.920
So what made you change your mind?

20:06.920 --> 20:08.360
Hmm...

20:09.870 --> 20:15.030
Because I wanted to be able to spend 
as much time with you as I can.

20:18.360 --> 20:22.940
F-Fuyuki-san, you're sure 
teasing me extra hard today.

20:22.940 --> 20:27.050
<i>Back when I first got here, a line 
like that would've finished me off!</i>

20:27.050 --> 20:27.850
Huh?

20:28.190 --> 20:30.500
I haven't teased you about anything today.

20:33.290 --> 20:35.570
I've been totally serious.

20:41.850 --> 20:42.620
Fuyuki—

20:42.620 --> 20:46.140
Hello, you two! Are you about to finish soon?

20:46.450 --> 20:49.860
If it's going to take much 
longer, I could help out.

20:49.860 --> 20:52.390
That's all right! We just finished.

20:52.630 --> 20:55.010
Oh, that's wonderful!

20:55.930 --> 20:57.440
No prob, no prob.

20:59.210 --> 21:03.980
Shiki-kun, Fuyuki-san, I'm so glad you 
decided to become the class representatives.

21:03.980 --> 21:05.030
Thanks for your hard work!

21:05.030 --> 21:06.300
Thank you, too!

21:06.300 --> 21:08.280
See you, Teach!

21:13.540 --> 21:16.270
It really is still cold at night.

21:16.270 --> 21:18.670
I guess there's still some winter left.

21:18.670 --> 21:19.590
Hmm.

21:19.590 --> 21:20.460
Huh?

21:32.210 --> 21:36.050
<i>She seems really down. And after 
the constant teasing today...</i>

21:36.050 --> 21:38.220
<i>I wonder what's gotten into her.</i>

21:40.380 --> 21:41.400
Tsubasa.

21:42.130 --> 21:42.940
Yes?

21:43.940 --> 21:45.980
Golden Week is next month.

21:46.700 --> 21:49.850
It doesn't matter which one, but would 
you keep one whole day free for me?

21:49.850 --> 21:50.490
Huh?

21:51.480 --> 21:54.570
I have something that I want to tell you.

21:57.710 --> 21:58.420
Oh...

22:00.320 --> 22:02.060
M'kay, then. See you.

22:04.340 --> 22:05.050
Uh...

22:11.320 --> 22:15.400
I've never seen Fuyuki-san 
get so serious before.

22:17.360 --> 22:18.750
<i>As the season turns to spring,</i>

22:19.530 --> 22:22.560
<i>the Hokkaido snow has started to clear up,</i>

22:23.710 --> 22:25.540
<i>but everything inside my head</i>

22:26.140 --> 22:27.330
<i>is still a white blur.</i>
